From: Alp Lab AB <contact@alplab.ai>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 01:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: tas2562: reset the amplifier at probe
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Copyright (c) 2026 Alp Lab AB
SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0

The driver's register cache starts from the POR defaults, including
PAGE_CTRL = 0, but the probe path never puts the silicon in that state.
When the part was not power-cycled -- a warm reboot with SD_N held high,
which is what happens on the E1M-X-EVK where SD_N is one shared net for
both TAS2563 amps -- it keeps the previous kernel's book, page and
configuration.  regmap then skips the page-select write (the cached
selector already reads 0), so page-0 writes land in whatever page was
left selected (page 2, after any Digital Volume change), and cached
writes that match the stale defaults are dropped as no-ops.

Seen on an E1M-V2M103 bench board after `reboot -f`: PB_CFG1 kept the
previous boot's amplifier level while the cache said 0x00, so
"Amp Gain Volume" writes silently did nothing, and the TDM slot width
set by set_tdm_slot never reached TDM_CFG2.

Select book 0 / page 0 with the cache bypassed and issue SW_RESET before
registering the component, then wait for the reset to complete.

--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2562.c
@@ -23,6 +23,8 @@
 
 #include "tas2562.h"
 
+#define TAS2562_BOOK_CTRL	TAS2562_REG(0, 0x7f)
+
 #define TAS2562_FORMATS (SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S16_LE | SNDRV_PCM_FMTBIT_S24_LE |\
 			 SNDRV_PCM_FORMAT_S32_LE)
 
@@ -756,6 +758,30 @@
 
 	dev_set_drvdata(&client->dev, data);
 
+	/*
+	 * A warm reboot does not necessarily pass through SD_N (the line can
+	 * be pulled high on the board or shared with another amplifier), so
+	 * the device may come up still holding the previous kernel's book,
+	 * page and configuration.  The register cache starts from the POR
+	 * defaults -- including PAGE_CTRL = 0, which makes regmap skip the
+	 * page-select write -- so every access would land in whatever page
+	 * was left selected.  Select book 0 / page 0 with the cache bypassed
+	 * and issue a software reset so the silicon matches the cache.
+	 */
+	regcache_cache_bypass(data->regmap, true);
+	ret = regmap_write(data->regmap, TAS2562_PAGE_CTRL, 0x00);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = regmap_write(data->regmap, TAS2562_BOOK_CTRL, 0x00);
+	if (!ret)
+		ret = regmap_write(data->regmap, TAS2562_SW_RESET, 0x01);
+	regcache_cache_bypass(data->regmap, false);
+	if (ret) {
+		dev_err(dev, "failed to reset device: %d\n", ret);
+		return ret;
+	}
+	/* Allow the reset to complete before the first cached access. */
+	usleep_range(1000, 2000);
+
 	if (data->model_id == TAS2110)
 		return devm_snd_soc_register_component(dev,
 						       &soc_component_dev_tas2110,
-- 
2.43.0
